          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            %strong Hecke algebra
            is a term for a class of
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/algebras"} algebras
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/convolution+algebras"} convolution algebras
            or as double
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coset+spaces"} coset spaces
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+algebra"} Lie algebra
            plays in the complex case (the Lie algebra still exists, but is too small).
          %p
            Typically the term refers to an algebra which is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/endomorphisms"} endomorphisms
            of a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/permutation+representation"} permutation representation
            of a
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+group"} topological group
          %p For example:
          %ul
            %li
              If we consider the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/general+linear+group"} general linear group
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi GL
                      %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi 𝔽
                      %mi q
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} GL_n(\mathbb{F}_q)
              acting on the set of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/flag"} complete flags
              in
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msubsup
                        %mi 𝔽
                        %mi q
                        %mi n
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{F}_q^n
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi σ
                      %mi i
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \sigma_i
              which sends the characteristic function of one flag
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi F
                    %mo =
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %msub
                      %mi F
                      %mn 1
                    %mo ⊂
                    %mi ⋯
                    %mo ⊂
                    %msub
                      %mi F
                      %mrow
                        %mi n
                        %mo −
                        %mn 1
                    %mo ⊂
                    %msubsup
                      %mi 𝔽
                      %mi q
                      %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{F}=\{F_1\subset \cdots \subset F_{n-1}\subset \mathbb{F}_q^n\}
              to the characteristic function of the set of flags
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
